WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.281
In this lesson we use IF in a calculated column.

2
00:00:04.281 --> 00:00:08.440
In Table view, on the Shipments table, I click New column.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.627
The column is called SP01 Cancelled.

4
00:00:14.627 --> 00:00:16.378
IF has three parts:

5
00:00:16.378 --> 00:00:21.631
a logical test, the value if true, and the value if false.

6
00:00:21.631 --> 00:00:26.009
If the order status is Cancelled, return Ask the Reason.

7
00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:27.760
Otherwise, return Leave It.

8
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.220
Now we add a second condition:

9
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.180
the salesperson must be S P zero one.

10
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.510
To test two things at once, we use AND.

11
00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.840
AND checks whether all of its arguments are true.

12
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.194
The AND function accepts only two arguments, and it must sit inside the IF

13
00:01:11.194 --> 00:01:13.050
test, before the first comma.

14
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.760
Putting it in the wrong place is a common error.

15
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.397
Instead of the AND function, you can use the double ampersand operator.

16
00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:41.160
It means the same thing, and it can join more than two conditions.

17
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.253
For OR, use the double pipe operator, or the OR function.

18
00:02:02.253 --> 00:02:06.120
OR returns true when at least one condition is true.

19
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.169
Calculated columns like this are a simple way to flag rows that need follow up.

20
00:02:34.169 --> 00:02:39.926
In monitoring work, the same idea flags late reports, missing data, or sites that

21
00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.160
need a visit.

